description:
Design a simple Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) generator. The module produces a PWM output signal, pwm_o, that is HIGH when a counter (cnt) is less than a specified threshold value. The counter increments on each rising edge of the input clock signal clk_i, allowing the duty cycle of the PWM signal to be controlled by the 8-bit threshold input. When the counter reaches the threshold, the output transitions to LOW, creating a periodic square wave with a variable duty cycle based on the threshold value.
module top_module(
    clk_i,
    pwm_o,
    threshold
);

code:
module top_module(
    clk_i,
    pwm_o,
    threshold
);input clk_i;
output pwm_o;
wire pwm_o;
input [7:0] threshold;

reg [7:0] cnt;




assign pwm_o = (cnt < threshold);


always @(posedge clk_i) begin: PWM_SIMPLE_LOC_INSTS_CHUNK_INSTS_K
    cnt <= (cnt + 1);
end

endmodule

