description:
Create a glitch filter that stabilizes the input signal by implementing a shift register. The module samples the input signal over a specified number of clock cycles (defined by the parameter n) and compares the current shift register value to the expected pattern of stable input. If the input remains consistent for the entire duration (n cycles), the output reflects the stable input signal; otherwise, it outputs the last known stable value from the previous cycles to mitigate transient fluctuations or glitches in the input.
module top_module(
  input clk,        // Added clock input
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,        // Added clock input
  input in,
  output out
);parameter n = 4; // number of clock cycles for glitch filter

reg [n-1:0] shift_reg;
reg [n-1:0] prev_values;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  shift_reg <= {shift_reg[n-2:0], in};
  prev_values <= {prev_values[n-2:0], shift_reg[0]};
end

assign out = (shift_reg == {n{in}}) ? in : prev_values[0];

endmodule

