description:
Design a clock divider module that takes an input clock signal and outputs a divided clock signal (clock_out). The module uses a 2-bit counter to toggle the output clock signal on every second rising edge of the input clock, effectively reducing the frequency by a factor of 2. The output will also be reset to LOW when the reset signal is asserted, allowing for a controlled initialization of the clock output.
module top_module(
    input clock,
    input reset,
    output reg clock_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clock,
    input reset,
    output reg clock_out
);reg [1:0] count;

always @(posedge clock or posedge reset) begin
    if (reset) begin
        count <= 2'b00;
        clock_out <= 1'b0;
    end
    else begin
        count <= count + 1;
        if (count == 2'b01) begin
            clock_out <= ~clock_out;
        end
    end
end

endmodule

