description:
Design a debouncing circuit for a noisy input signal, typically from a mechanical switch, using a clock signal for synchronization. The circuit utilizes a counter to determine periods of stability in the noisy input, updating three state registers (d1, d2, d3) only after a specified counter threshold is met. The final debounced output is asserted when all three registers agree, ensuring that the output changes only when the input remains stable, thus effectively filtering out transient noise caused by switch bounce.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input noisy,
  output debounced
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input noisy,
  output debounced
);assign debounced = d1 & d2 & d3;

reg [18:0] counter;
reg d1, d2, d3;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (&counter) begin
    counter <= 19'b0;
    d1 <= noisy;
    d2 <= d1;
    d3 <= d2;
  end else
    counter <= counter + 1'b1;
end

endmodule

