Design a delay line circuit that introduces a delay of a specified number of clock cycles (d) to an input signal. The module captures the input on each rising edge of the clock and shifts it through a buffer of d bits. The output provides the value of the input that was received d clock cycles prior, effectively creating a delay in the output signal relative to the input.
